A class Constructor that returns a value (diag.constructor_return_value,
error). Near misses in the same class: a bare :RETURN; early exit in the
Constructor and :RETURN with a value from an ordinary method.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Gauge;
:DECLARE nLevel;

:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	:PARAMETERS nStart;
	:IF Empty(nStart);
		Me:nLevel := 0;
		:RETURN;
	:ENDIF;
	Me:nLevel := nStart;
	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Level;
	:RETURN Me:nLevel;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Gauge;
:DECLARE nLevel;

:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	:PARAMETERS nStart;
	:IF Empty(nStart);
		Me:nLevel := 0;
		:RETURN;
	:ENDIF;
	Me:nLevel := nStart;
	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Level;
	:RETURN Me:nLevel;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
11:2-11:9 error constructor_return_value: ':RETURN' inside a Constructor cannot return a value
